    "body": "> This links to the heading, but it seems the algorithm uses process-policy-attributes.\r\n\r\nOops good catch!\r\n\r\n> Did we always link this incorrectly or did they regress? If it's the latter arguably they should fix this as links should be ~forever.\r\n\r\nI think they regressed. But it looks like it was a while ago: https://github.com/w3c/webappsec-permissions-policy/commit/d2b4fd56e2406fd8fb321681397ed83babbbc473#diff-5e793325cd2bfc452e268a4aa2f02b4024dd9584bd1db3c2595f61f1ecf7b985L847-L848 (L847 on the deletion side; the link doesn't seem to drag you down to the right anchor). So I guess this is technically their fault, but it's a very old error, so we should just fix our side IMO.",
